    "text": "Step 2: Determine the coordinates of the foci. For an ellipse \\(\\frac{x^2}{a^2} + \\frac{y^2}{b^2} = 1\\) with \\(a > b\\), the distance from the center to each focus is \\(c = \\sqrt{a^2 - b^2}\\). Here, \\(a = 1\\) and \\(b = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{k}}\\), so \\(c = \\sqrt{1 - \\frac{1}{k}}\\). Therefore, the foci are at \\((\\pm \\sqrt{1 - \\frac{1}{k}}, 0)\\)."
